{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22722081","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.22722081","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.22722081","identifiers":[{"identifier":"oai:zenodo.org:22722081","identifierType":"oai"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"oai","alternateIdentifier":"oai:zenodo.org:22722081"}],"creators":[{"name":"Jayadevan, Achyuth","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Achyuth","familyName":"Jayadevan","affiliation":["Manipal Institute of Technology, MAHE"],"nameIdentifiers":[{"nameIdentifier":"0009-0008-8745-4078","nameIdentifierScheme":"ORCID"}]}],"titles":[{"title":"HNN extensions and inner homogeneity of group representations over commutative rings"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"Kourovka Problem 17.101"},{"subject":"Group representations"},{"subject":"HNN extensions"},{"subject":"Homogeneous representations"},{"subject":"Commutative rings"},{"subject":"Lean 4"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-09-12","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":"en","types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsVersionOf","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.22722080","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1.0.0","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"},{"rights":"Copyright © 2026 Achyuth Jayadevan.","rightsUri":"http://rightsstatements.org/vocab/InC/1.0/"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Let \\(R\\) be a nonzero commutative ring. Every \\(R\\)-representation \\((G,V)\\) embeds in \\((\\Gamma,W)\\) with \\[\\ker\\bigl(\\Gamma\\to\\operatorname{Aut}_R(W)\\bigr)=1,\\qquad |\\Gamma|,|W|\\le\\max\\{\\aleph_0,|R|,|G|,|V|\\},\\] such that every isomorphism between finitely generated subrepresentations is induced by \\((g\\mapsto tgt^{-1},\\,w\\mapsto tw)\\) for some \\(t\\in\\Gamma\\). A local HNN construction realizes arbitrary subrepresentation isomorphisms by adjoining the corresponding linear relations to an induced module. Injectivity follows from the boundary map of a tree of modules, with no splitting or projectivity assumption. The field case answers Kourovka Problem 17.101.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722081","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-09-14T16:06:19.000Z","registered":"2026-09-14T16:06:19.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-09-14T16:06:19.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22722081","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22722080","type":"dois"}]}}}}